  "run": {
    "status": "completed",
    "answer": "Reviewed the household records and transaction leads. No prior open work was found.\n\n- **ShopMart:** Submitted request **SM-1001** for the missing **$30.37** refund on return SM-50937; no matching credit appeared in the available transactions. Submitted request **SM-1002** to investigate the second **$104.16** charge on August 21, supported by an order email listing one order that day. Follow-ups are scheduled for October 20.\n- **CloudBox:** A **$59.99** annual renewal posted October 1. The stated 14-day refund window ended October 15. I submitted billing case **CB-1003** asking for a goodwill refund and scheduled a follow-up for October 20. The note says the service is no longer needed, so I saved a waiting approval request to cancel CloudBox Plus. **Your approval is needed to cancel.**\n- **Other recurring charges:** Reviewed Metro Power, Spotify, and Oakview Apartments transaction histories; found no related source note saying these services are unwanted.\n\nThe review status reports no remaining items. No refund has been confirmed as received.",
    "committed_micros": 32003
  },
  "verify_run": {
    "status": "completed",
    "answer": "The review is complete. ShopMart\u2019s duplicate-charge refund ($104.16) and return refund ($30.37), plus CloudBox\u2019s annual-plan refund ($59.99), all appear as posted credits dated October 15. I recorded each as received with transaction evidence.\n\nThe ShopMart duplicate request was already submitted. CloudBox\u2019s refund request was also submitted, and its reply says the account is closed. The existing approval request to cancel CloudBox remains in the records; no further action is needed for that closure. No new fee, price increase, or credit-promise leads were found. The recurring charges are Spotify, Metro Power, and Oakview rent; no note says they\u2019re unwanted.\n\nThe review checklist reports no remaining work.",
    "committed_micros": 9940
  },
